auth	desc	Inspect permissions: who this credential is, what it holds, what routes need
auth	help	
auth	examples	
auth grant	desc	Renew a grant that is still in force (creation and revoking happen on the web console)
auth grant	help	
auth grant	examples	
auth grant renew	desc	Give a session grant more time: renew <grant-id> --for <dur> (at most 24h)
auth grant renew	help	Pushes back the deadline of a session grant that is still in force: the new deadline is now
plus --for, at most 24 hours. Only the deadline moves — the granted pattern, what it expands to,
the grantor and the session it is bound to all stay as they are, so a renewal cannot widen a grant.

A grant that already expired, was revoked, no longer matches any permission, or whose session
ended (or changed owner / incarnation) cannot be renewed: the server refuses it and this command
prints its reason — grant it again from the web console instead.

  gofer auth grant renew g-1a2b3c --for 4h
  gofer auth grant renew g-1a2b3c --for 90m
auth grant renew	examples	
auth grant renew	flag config	path to the gofer config file
auth grant renew	flag for	how much longer the grant should last, from now (e.g. 4h, 90m; at most 24h)
auth grant renew	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
auth grant renew	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
auth routes	desc	List the server's routes and the permissions each one needs
auth routes	help	Prints every route of the running server with its declaration: who may call it
(require / in_handler / public / no_user_surface), the permissions it asks for, and which other
credential reaches it (a job credential, a worker token, or the route's own ticket / token).

  gofer auth routes
auth routes	examples	
auth routes	flag config	path to the gofer config file
auth routes	flag json	print the server's answer as JSON
auth routes	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
auth routes	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
auth whoami	desc	Show which caller this credential is and the permissions it holds
auth whoami	help	Prints the caller id, whether it is a root administrator, every permission it holds with
its source (root / config / db) and the grant a database permission came from.

The request carries the terminal session this process belongs to, when the environment names
exactly one of them ($GOFER_SESSION_ID explicitly, or a single agent session variable); the
session grants that apply to it are part of the permissions printed, and the session and its
source are named in the output. With no session, or with several candidates that disagree,
nothing is attached — a request never guesses a session.

  gofer auth whoami
  gofer auth whoami --json
auth whoami	examples	
auth whoami	flag config	path to the gofer config file
auth whoami	flag json	print the server's answer as JSON
auth whoami	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
auth whoami	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
