repo	desc	Manage this repository's local tracker
repo	help	
repo	examples	
repo changelog-merge	desc	Git merge driver for a Keep a Changelog CHANGELOG.md (merges the unreleased section); --install sets it up in this clone
repo changelog-merge	help	git runs it as `gofer repo changelog-merge %O %A %B %P` (base, ours, theirs, path); the result
replaces <ours>. Only the unreleased section is auto-merged: its `### ` subsections merge per
entry — ours keeps the entry order, theirs' new entries (multi-line and nested ones included)
are appended in theirs' order, an entry deleted on the other untouched side disappears, an
entry changed on one side only takes that side's text (a new entry next to it is not a change
of it), an entry changed differently on both sides becomes a conflict marker. A subsection
only one side added is kept whole. The header and the released versions go through
`git merge-file`, so a region both sides changed comes back with git's standard conflict
markers and a non-zero exit.
When one side released (renamed the unreleased heading to a version and opened a new
unreleased section) while the other added entries, the new entries land in the new section.

--install appends `<file> merge=gofer-changelog` to .gitattributes (commit it) and
sets merge.gofer-changelog.{name,driver} in the clone's git config, which every worktree of
the clone shares. Each new clone runs --install once.
repo changelog-merge	examples	
repo changelog-merge	flag config	path to the gofer config file
repo changelog-merge	flag file	changelog path relative to the repository root (--install)
repo changelog-merge	flag install	configure the driver for this repository (.gitattributes + git config) instead of merging
repo changelog-merge	flag unreleased	comma-separated section titles treated as unreleased (default: 未发布,Unreleased)
repo init	desc	Initialize local issue and memory files
repo init	help	
repo init	examples	
repo init	flag commit-policy	set commit_policy: local-commit | ask | none (default: keep the current value; a new tracker gets local-commit)
repo init	flag config	path to the gofer config file
repo init	flag no-agents-md	do not write a managed agent instruction block
repo init	flag no-hooks	do not install the session-start prime and command-memory hooks (.claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json)
repo init	flag prefix	issue id prefix (default: repository directory name)
repo init	flag tracker	explicit .gofer/tracker directory
repo merge-driver	desc	Git merge driver for .gofer/tracker/*.jsonl (merges records by id); --install sets it up in this clone
repo merge-driver	help	git runs it as `gofer repo merge-driver %O %A %B %P` (base, ours, theirs, path); the result
replaces <ours>. Records merge by issue id / memory key: one-sided adds, edits and deletes are
taken; a record edited on both sides merges field by field (a field both changed takes the side
with the newer updated_at), comments / notes / tags / deps are unioned; delete vs edit keeps the
edit. Decisions between two real edits are printed to stderr. A file it cannot read safely falls
back to git's text merge (conflict markers, non-zero exit).

--install (also run by `gofer repo init`) appends `.gofer/tracker/*.jsonl merge=gofer-tracker`
to .gitattributes (commit it) and sets merge.gofer-tracker.{name,driver} in the clone's
git config, which every worktree of the clone shares. Each new clone runs --install once.
repo merge-driver	examples	
repo merge-driver	flag config	path to the gofer config file
repo merge-driver	flag install	configure the driver for this repository (.gitattributes + git config) instead of merging
repo migrate	desc	Migrate a bd (beads) repository to the gofer tracker (dry-run unless --apply)
repo migrate	help	Reads the live bd database (`bd export`, read-only; .beads/issues.jsonl only as a fallback) and
imports issues + memories into .gofer/tracker, then swaps the bd integration points: the BEADS
blocks in AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md become the gofer block, `bd prime` / `bd codex-hook` hooks become
`gofer repo prime --hook-json`, and core.hooksPath is unset when it points at .beads/hooks and
that directory holds only bd's own hooks. .beads/ is kept. Anything else that mentions bd is
listed for a human. --apply refuses while bd looks active (locks, processes, writes in the last
minutes, unexpired claim leases); --force overrides.
repo migrate	examples	
repo migrate	flag apply	apply changes (default: dry-run)
repo migrate	flag config	path to the gofer config file
repo migrate	flag force	apply even though bd looks active
repo migrate	flag from-bd	migrate from bd (required)
repo migrate	flag json	print the report as JSON
