settings import	desc	Apply a YAML settings file (dry run: shows every key's change first)
settings import	help	Every key is reported: set / reset / unchanged, and the reason a refused key was
refused. WITHOUT --yes nothing is written (the server runs the same validation in its
dry-run mode), so the default is a safe preview:

  gofer settings import backup.yaml            # preview
  gofer settings import backup.yaml --yes      # write
  gofer settings export | gofer settings import - --yes
settings import	examples	
settings import	flag config	path to the gofer config file
settings import	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
settings import	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
settings import	flag yes	write the values instead of printing the preview
settings ls	desc	List every registered setting (key, type, whether it was changed, current value)
settings ls	help	The keys are whatever this server registers: the noise-reduction thresholds and
exclusion lists, and the prompt overrides. "changed" means a value is stored for the
key; an unchanged key follows the binary's default.
settings ls	examples	
settings ls	flag config	path to the gofer config file
settings ls	flag json	print the full entries as JSON instead of a table
settings ls	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
settings ls	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
