tool	desc	Small utilities: a raw API call, file copy to/from a worker, the transfer staging area, certificates and the stats backfill
tool	help	
tool	examples	
tool api	desc	Call the server's HTTP API and print the response (address and token included)
tool api	help	The path is relative to the server's /v1 API, so "jobs" and "/v1/jobs" are the
same request. The address and token come from the same place as everywhere else in the
CLI (-c / --server / --token, or $GOFER_CONFIG_DIR/.env), so nothing has to be typed
twice.

Fields build the body (`application/json`); on a GET they become query parameters
instead. A value is read as JSON when it parses as one (10 → number, true → bool) and as
a plain string otherwise:

  gofer tool api jobs -f status=running -f limit=5
  gofer tool api jobs -X POST --input job.json
  gofer tool api settings/work.draft.min_prompts -X PUT -f value=3
  gofer tool api prompt -F value=@prompt.md          # file content as a string
  gofer tool api jobs -q 'jobs.*.id'

--query picks one value out of the JSON response by path (top.sub, jobs.0.id,
jobs.*.id): a string prints as it is, anything else as indented JSON. A non-2xx answer
exits non-zero and prints the body to stderr; --include also shows the status line and
the response headers.
tool api	examples	
tool api	flag config	path to the gofer config file
tool api	flag field	field as key=value (repeatable; query parameters on a GET)
tool api	flag file-field	field as key=@file, the file's content as the string value (repeatable)
tool api	flag include	print the status line and response headers
tool api	flag input	raw request body from this file ('-' reads stdin)
tool api	flag query	print this value of the JSON response instead of the whole body
tool api	flag request	HTTP method (default: GET, or POST when a body is given)
tool api	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
tool api	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
